            "title": "Commerce Secretary Wilbur Ross Discusses China Trade Visit... - ...",
            "snippets": [
              "# Commerce Secretary Wilbur Ross Discusses China Trade Visit…\nMay 1, 2018 | Sundance | 164 Comments\n\nCommerce Secretary Wilbur Ross discusses the ongoing trade initiatives with China ahead of the U.S. delegation departing later tonight.  Secretary Ross, Treasury Secretary Mnuchin, U.S. Trade Representative/Ambassador Robert Lighthizer, Economic Council Chairman Larry Kudlow and White House Trade Adviser Peter Navarro are all heading to Beijing to meet with their Chinese counterparts",
              "Delegation heading to China to begin talks on the Massive Trade Deficit that has been created with our Country. Very much like North Korea, this should have been fixed years ago, not now. Same with other countries and NAFTA…but it will all get done. Great Potential for USA!"
            ]
          },
          {
            "url": "https://www.dailymail.com/news/article-5678407/Trump-sends-economic-team-China-talks-amid-trade-war-stand-off.html",
            "title": "Trump sends economic team to China for talks amid trade war stand-off",
            "snippets": [
              "# We'll get it done! Trump sends his economic team to China for talks amid trade war stand-off: 'This should have been fixed years ago'\n- **Treasury Secretary Steven Mnuchin and chief economic advisor Larry Kudlow will be among the U.S. officials on at the negotiating table in China**\n- **Talks will take place on Thursday and Friday in Beijing**\n- **'Very much like North Korea, this should have been fixed years ago, not now,' Trump said Tuesday of the wide trade deficit with China**",
              "50\nView comments\n\nPresident Trump is sending his economic team to Beijing for a stare down on trade",
              "Treasury Secretary Steven Mnuchin and Commerce Secretary Wilbur Ross will be among the U.S. officials on at the negotiating table in China, the White House said in a statement on Monday evening",
              "'Very much like North Korea, this should have been fixed years ago, not now,' he said Tuesday of the United States' wide trade deficit with China. 'Same with other countries and NAFTA...but it will all get done. Great Potential for USA!'\n\nPresident Trump is sending his economic team to Beijing for a stare down on trade\n\nPresident Trump is sending his economic team to Beijing for a stare down on trade",
              "Treasury Secretary Steven Mnuchin and Chief Economic advisor Larry Kudlow (left) will be among the U.S. officials on at the negotiating table in China\n\nThe U.S. and China have been in a stand-off that threatened to escalate in a full-blown trade war since Trump announced $50 billion of tariffs on Chinese imports",
              "After Xi Jinping's government threatened to hit the U.S. with retaliatory measures, Trump said he'd slap another $100 billion in penalties on Chinese-made goods if Beijing didn't stand down.\n\nXi has since offered concessions to the U.S., saying that he will ease tariffs on automobiles and introduce stricter intellectual property protections",
              "At the same time, China escalated a separate dispute with the U.S. over Trump's worldwide steel and aluminum tariffs to the World Trade Organization.\n\nIn a Fox Business appearance this week, Mnuchin said that a trade war is 'not a worry of mine' and that Trump merely wants 'free and fair and reciprocal trade.'\n\nMnuchin said he expected to have 'very frank discussions' with the Chinese this week in Beijing",
              "## Share this article\nShare\n\nU.S. officials will be in Beijing on Thursday and Friday.\n\n'We're looking to have a very frank discussion on trade, on the issues of the trade imbalance,' Mnuchin said Monday.\n\nLarry Kudlow, the president's chief economic advisor, will also participate in talks",
              "U.S. Trade Representative Robert Lighthizer and Trump's senior trade adviser Peter Navarro will also be a part of the U.S. delegation, as will U.S. Ambassador to China Terry Branstad, the White House says.\n\nChinese Vice Premier Liu He will be representing Beijing."
            ]
          },
